AJyN51a3cGb0ygoQ_PFrwgBPqK2ApLY6L2q2JL_6tiChEK70V1eNFgYU26PGwb67ZeYW6TgPhkm=
QCV_Ygg74JQi4qKSG0bC3AT6zLswthrfCG_qP9ACj84wg_h2ULg9ieGzKV-tjFIMEgC41O5Fg/4=
uj/UousbppZQDqzP7AgYzkUDg/h28/h001.kwFNbavtkuf84zaY9oNx1EVGf3RYfJ5NEfluFmES=
nsg" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">after leaking out</a>, the Manchester City s=
aga has become a flood. Peace in our time has disappeared into the distance=
 as football jurisprudence=E2=80=99s longest-running case enters Defcon 1 l=
awfare. Football Daily is duty bound by its learned friends in the legal de=
partment who gamely pick through this cheery teatime email before it reache=
s you, to say that City continue to deny all charges [we don=E2=80=99t nece=
ssarily need this but we=E2=80=99re happy to remain the butt of the joke =
=E2=80=93 Football Daily Lawyers]. Though that also serves as a statement o=
f the bleeding obvious. Club operatives and associates have employed not so=
 much a double but a nonuple-down. The expected appeal <a href=3D"https://a=
blink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMg=
szcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgJBqVb-v-SZiam8iyhBbYhoFX1v-pZbjfplgg5Upz3SXJ=
VJwXikP1yU8VMqegAl2c_JtsXIgsF1ISpaedieCtco124WbkZpZ-ZxhDt2XRzGPuJlds0oySfwc=
wSQRJJsRAa28NMcclfy48XcHzuaga1fzWR3aG7M_G3cokE32LbJzV0Pf3dPnO1FARUua53dQGnZ=
UnsSVmBIfYa8RrWNn_s3g5v5VJUpDbE2mZfdC7HdU/4uj/UousbppZQDqzP7AgYzkUDg/h29/h0=
01.S9zJIy0bPIc7UCl08iGzjcH_NAopQobXKfnTxgOgweU" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">h=
as now been lodged</a> by City. The statement was as you=E2=80=99d expect: =
=E2=80=9CThe club is innocent of the accusations made by the Premier League=
 and a comprehensive body of irrefutable evidence exists in support of all =
of its positions, relating to this case.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The challenge to the Premier League=E2=80=
=99s published, contested verdict has already reached the levels of bringin=
g your dinner to the fight. City=E2=80=99s key sponsor, Etihad Airways, <a =
href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_X=
G18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg0kKvhiUMljqZrPeZCmf22qQqBqi=
l-KkjM7cybyD0734eOQ1yKXFJ0el2peUEPaHZKA__Bs_12p_ESBHRfvK-ROwNnrO48dzylcrW5N=
UTGGuBXOmN5MR1kAMZUUtQqZjkw7_LrovM3UggGVU8KKj9s4hrG-OPpxKJOhmsPrJRww1_nktmU=
xn7-4mNastkRgNrJ6e_1IXg-qlgaPnd0ZrwBVArEqKma_Et5caxhdMAjlqwGphZgBxBBrBQ7xNw=
lMbt/4uj/UousbppZQDqzP7AgYzkUDg/h30/h001.Ll843lS-Wn_Jy2Jqou7Gft8xIOQdlWbrdM=
sroUmGd_E" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">is getting involved</a>, with reports =
suggesting it is appointing a law firm that received a =E2=80=9Cmost feared=
=E2=80=9D industry gong five years in a row to state its case. Yikes! Even =
Pep Guardiola only managed four titles on the bounce. These days Guardiola =
is global ambassador for the City Football Group. As such, he has <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18I=
RyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgBiQ7-aicYlGLUqrYBHOjimPWezLGYuU=
g3zIP59wiVFGeduB1fUgvdUcfm8V1uBSSv2Ba2Fcmg2Sbb8ivtVojInbS4RgBGitKVcR_yE9ujX=
_QyKdSp43U2YS8FYXVcIpsgEPV_x1lDG1SR3dgRVN4xg9friTfDlwDCstWG_WJh-Eu2TEDXmy9x=
YYUqRZ904l2rdrSZqJIKBlRPpRuC-ZvFKz8yO-Z06a2So7jDxrV0CPjgB-EaIQ0qgQoDz4AEG5q=
/4uj/UousbppZQDqzP7AgYzkUDg/h31/h001.C95v4OOlF2fOuobcRPO4K9GI6K0ETT0u9zJ_GB=
daVvs" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">already joined</a> Liam Gallagher and Curl=
y Watts actor Kevin Kennedy in fighting from the blue corner on social medi=
a disgraces boiling with militant fans arguing points of commercial law whi=
le decrying =E2=80=9Cthe Red Cartel=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">With each hour has come a plot twist in th=
e fight against the verdict that unblinking club suit Ferran Soriano descri=
bed via video link to staff as a mere =E2=80=9Copinion=E2=80=9D, which fed =
into a =E2=80=9C<a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u0=
01.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgeL94mxcX=
9c0olhmChWavhlZ_oduo2m4IOojwIPZGOXQSBnlKK0Mlg97I07-QuWS73IhfTUZurg1oqajLCy3=
Gj026rVEobjZhLRABzJXUGoK4Pwp8BbYu8qv9vPgHdNvDhnqsTTXjFn3xakECBRhWqzWeHE7Y-Z=
jSY7-3KuL93oqzeJZkoBuifBYR5uJR-lmxFTtaAvdqdhAPXoVcl6Q-HXgOPMGAXA_NY7ftOaE1S=
ac4PrrGNZm6TBgI-Zv-1YhRLYHBkJS1QYhyIog7Bxt14Q/4uj/UousbppZQDqzP7AgYzkUDg/h3=
2/h001.xYU_R5TjyHqrusNbGsAYfLyaJhP8-E4BlrLLkFICR-w" style=3D"color: #0077B6=
;">Premier League conspiracy theory</a>=E2=80=9D. Contrary to previous push=
ing back =E2=80=93 <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c=
/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBHiUlCFBczxKFujAbrhIe_vE7DT=
6IQki0N2GNbN6h6-njAX2za1g-OwtNf6nfERe62Gyw61HpTZG7dw1hKXUyrDipafyXRcH2C3t5V=
Yed_e6Qng4uDTL2Ed4YFNjU9BHdT4Rj3Voq7XHsQXSVp9H7gO21WVZPHWcFBCdo79ubVjQ2nl_y=
qdCYNEAFTe0qWaNZAEpf5RCvlKnuoky7xJ-2ymMqbvR8Kt0JTD32nZ_l4xA/4uj/UousbppZQDq=
zP7AgYzkUDg/h33/h001.cdXRy0U0CjyR7Aw5A9kDJstXOF3BFpsRYk3yORTzb9U" style=3D"=
color: #0077B6;">since 2008</a> =E2=80=93 against City being depicted as a =
state-owned entity on the grounds that Sheikh Mansour=E2=80=99s ownership w=
as as a private individual, came the revelation the money inflating City=E2=
=80=99s sponsorship coffers came not via Mansour=E2=80=99s investment vehic=
le but the Abu Dhabi state government. This, say the legal experts =E2=80=
=93 and social media disgrace sleuths =E2=80=93 is likely to form =E2=80=9C=
the comprehensive body of irrefutable evidence=E2=80=9D that City=E2=80=99s=
 people argue is the winning hand. The original published verdict =E2=80=93=
 if redacted, sans appendices =E2=80=93 has already rejected that angle as =
=E2=80=9Cuntrue=E2=80=9D. Awkward. Further stirring of the hotpot: on Thurs=
day, the UK government=E2=80=99s treasury committee asked tax authorities w=
hat action will be taken in response to the verdict=E2=80=99s findings.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">All rather complicated, to the lawyers the=
 spoils. And from the soft power of owning a football club, the harsh reali=
ties of geopolitics have entered the chat. Prime minister Andy Burnham has =
had No 10 Downing Street wonks <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguard=
ian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDr=
a0BxnPg6X8_zc7Mwh9j8deYWVwZ-yRU1HTKdsiCk-KkqQTdoroBSGNlWOcnZege2MRXPzQzcYhp=
dCSxf3CmTZKys2ikaxNApJUnfTu4nr0xswaPN_ZYyd00Hhadppn-xwfvfbzCJdlx21ce9yztHtS=
CtXygP6Q7idxFVlQ-jANBogZuqj7YnvE7XKSLUnFU2sAgQZeqymta1xAenqJICM5IW5D3jQU3_L=
vwlmkPnPlo71EBB95rS9ef1hNrnssT-H-NBrLlPxdZOAkUk2F5ecv8REc5qg/4uj/UousbppZQD=
qzP7AgYzkUDg/h34/h001.IBnZPgwE4NwGFxJp_a3876t7h3jJlDnIywuGhVK7Bp4" style=3D=
"color: #0077B6;">issuing two clarifications</a> of his initial public utte=
rings on the City affair. Everton Andy=E2=80=99s Manchesterism involved key=
 partnerships with the same Abu Dhabi state government that now admits fund=
ing the club found guilty on 100-plus Premier League charges. Added to that=
, reports of potential political pressure on the UK government from Abu Dha=
bi, a key trading partner, and <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguard=
ian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDr=
a0BxnPg56XKPqqbPHxQ38BoXDZdOoZWV1MRDMp2FXvgzRNsRRPhrviwrM-TrTCs7J-q9TP7GVJW=
hpcQ1pStXgXwEoLUiOTKcY8gMEANYTkxMEmJukP-xz8FOdUuu70SVTwRXenOnsO7O-XwO1Xy3Vh=
6ryPnv0J0vmip94bd4_4IP233TlikYEwdDeV2IJLtQmXysmROZz7yybYahkQp9tUYoa-AZBSEI1=
0RG03u6F0K5hQq3LY/4uj/UousbppZQDqzP7AgYzkUDg/h35/h001.JrpWpQC5t7MSun4TrrmXX=
u1mWuiF2R7B1qvWpoN3swo" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">calls from the Liberal De=
mocrats</a> for Burnham to publish details of all his meetings with the clu=
b=E2=80=99s owners. Manchester City, so much to answer for.</p>
